#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:379
msgid ""
"``wrk`` keeps 64 requests in flight, so on the CPU-bound proxied paths "
"requests queue for the four CPUs, and the p99 there is the scheduler's "
"tail rather than the cost of one request. An open-loop generator, which "
"sends at a fixed rate and times each request from its intended send, "
"measures latency at equal offered load instead. For admitted requests in "
"reverse-proxy mode, the p99 is 65 us at 10,000 requests per second and "
"100 us at 100,000; at 150,000 offered the four CPUs saturate, 134,344 "
"requests per second are achieved, and the queue grows to seconds "
"(``benchmarks/results/latency-latest.md``). A warm keep-alive connection "
"serves every decision without a heap allocation: "
"``cmd/sibuna/tests/steady_state.rs`` counts the allocations of the "
"daemon, and ``crates/net/tests/steady_state.rs`` finds none over 500 "
"proxied keep-alive requests."
msgstr ""

